Um, you see, the reason I wanted to sing this song is because Iofi has a wish that I absolutely, no matter what, cannot give up.

141
00:23:06,754 --> 00:23:08,274
何が譲れなかったの？
What couldn't you give up?

142
00:23:09,474 --> 00:23:19,174
いや、多分ね、今回がひとつのステージ、こうやって歌いたいのが、あの初めからの話をお姉さんと。
Well, probably, this time being one stage, wanting to sing like this, um, talking from the beginning with big sister...

143
00:23:19,174 --> 00:23:28,394
そうだね、そう、ずっとやりたかったんだけど、で、今日、二人でいい曲、えっと、本当にね、ちょっと緊張したんだけど。
That's right, yeah, I've always wanted to do it, and today, singing a great song together, um, I was really a bit nervous.

144
00:23:28,394 --> 00:23:30,514
そうそうそう。全然、よかった！
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Not at all, it was great!

145
00:23:30,514 --> 00:23:31,854
すごいよかった！
It was really great!

146
00:23:31,854 --> 00:23:40,134
ありがとう！落としたらどうしようって。めっちゃめちゃ楽しかった！
Thank you! I was wondering what would happen if I dropped it. It was super, super fun!

147
00:23:40,134 --> 00:23:42,514
本当？ありがとう！嬉しい！
Really? Thank you! I'm so happy!

148
00:23:42,514 --> 00:23:49,334
でね、お姉さんね、あのね、ステージにお姉さんの絵が居るんですよ。
And you know, big sister, um, your picture is on the stage.

149
00:23:49,574 --> 00:23:52,514
ええ、じゃあどこかな？どこかな？
Eh, then where could it be? Where could it be?

150
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:59,774
こっちだったか！こっちだったかな？あ、いた！あ、いた！あ！
Was it this way? Was it this way? Oh, there she is! Oh, there she is! Ah!

151
00:23:59,774 --> 00:24:02,354
そう。ねえ、このステージにもお姉さん居るしね。
Right. Hey, you're on this stage too, big sister.

152
00:24:02,354 --> 00:24:07,434
ねえ、二人で仲良しだよ！仲良しだよ！やったあ！
Yeah, we're good friends together! Good friends! Yay!

153
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:14,614
ちなみにコメントのみんなは、ちょっと、見えた？という人がいるかな？
By the way, I wonder if anyone in the comments noticed or saw it?

154
00:24:15,234 --> 00:24:18,874
見えた！？みんな見えた！？見えたって！やったあ！
You saw it?! Everyone saw it?! They said they saw it! Yay!

155
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:22,974
いや、でも、それだけ私たちのことしっかり見てくれたってことだよ。
Yeah, but that just means they watched us really closely.

156
00:24:22,974 --> 00:24:24,534
ありがとうね。
Thank you.

157
00:24:24,534 --> 00:24:25,094
ありがとう！
Thank you!

158
00:24:27,114 --> 00:24:30,574
あのね、イオフィにね、プレゼントがあるんだ。
You know, I have a present for Iofi.

159
00:24:30,574 --> 00:24:33,014
なんだろ？なんだろ？なんだろね？
What could it be? What could it be? What could it be?

160
00:24:35,014 --> 00:24:37,334
これだー！
This is it!

161
00:24:38,514 --> 00:24:41,914
あれね、実はね、エフェ持てるんだ。え？
You know, actually, you can hold a paintbrush. Eh?

162
00:24:41,914 --> 00:24:43,974
ちょっとね、あれにぴったりのもの、うわ！
Something that fits that just right, whoa!

163
00:24:43,974 --> 00:24:46,494
おおー！ちょっとお姉さんの色を塗ってみようかな。
Ohh! Let me try painting it with big sister's colors.

164
00:24:46,494 --> 00:24:47,414
いやー！
No way!

165
00:24:47,414 --> 00:24:52,414
いいの？うわー！どうかな？うわ！
Is that okay? Whoa! How is it? Whoa!

166
00:24:52,414 --> 00:24:57,994
うおおー！増えた！増えたよー！
Uooo--! It increased! It increased!

167
00:24:57,994 --> 00:24:58,614
やったー！
Yay!

168
00:24:58,614 --> 00:24:59,714
ねえ！
Hey!

169
00:24:59,714 --> 00:25:01,994
ありがとうね。いやー、こっちだもーん。
Thank you. Man, this way~.

170
00:25:03,494 --> 00:25:04,774
じゃあこれはしまっておこうかな。
Well, I guess I'll put this away.

171
00:25:04,774 --> 00:25:05,894
ねえ、そうだね。大事な
Yeah, that's right. Important...

172
00:25:06,523 --> 00:25:09,603
また忘れちゃってたわ
I forgot again!

173
00:25:10,403 --> 00:25:14,123
まあこれからもまだまだということで
Well, there's still a lot more to come, so...

174
00:25:14,683 --> 00:25:17,083
うん、また会おうかなと。
Yeah, let's meet again sometime.

175
00:25:17,343 --> 00:25:19,943
そうだね、ゲストパートもまだまだ続くからね。
That's right, there are still more guest parts coming up!

176
00:25:20,343 --> 00:25:23,483
うん、またね、みんなー！
Yeah, see you again, everyone!

177
00:25:23,883 --> 00:25:25,023
じゃあねー！
Bye-bye!

178
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:29,963
じゃあねー！おめでとう！ありがとう！
Bye-bye! Congratulations! Thank you!

179
00:25:56,186 --> 00:25:58,986
[Title: One Night Carnival]

180
00:25:59,590 --> 00:26:00,190
Ah, yeah!

181
00:26:02,330 --> 00:26:02,990
Ah, yeah!

182
00:26:05,830 --> 00:26:06,550
Ah, yeah!

183
00:26:10,253 --> 00:26:13,233
真っ暗闇広がる群れの奥
Deep within the pitch-black darkness spreading out,

184
00:26:13,933 --> 00:26:16,513
好き好きとおどってるエンジェル
An angel dancing to whatever it likes.

185
00:26:18,413 --> 00:26:22,693
とにかくもう 優等生気取りなんてうんざりだった
Anyway, I was so sick of acting like a model student.

186
00:26:39,061 --> 00:26:43,581
退屈に怯えてたのさ 夜の闇に逃げ込んだ
Frightened by the boredom, I slipped away into the night's darkness.

187
00:26:45,101 --> 00:26:50,581
捨てどこみたいなおれたちに 帰る場所なんて もうどこにもなかった
For the likes of us, thrown away like garbage, there was nowhere left to go back to.

188
00:26:52,041 --> 00:26:55,881
エンジェル！Can you master baby? Master baby!
Angel! Can you master baby? Master baby!

189
00:26:56,181 --> 00:26:58,661
Can you master baby? Master baby!

190
00:26:59,181 --> 00:27:01,841
Can you master baby? Master baby!

191
00:27:03,281 --> 00:27:05,681
Can you master baby? Master baby, alone!

192
00:27:06,940 --> 00:27:10,940
瞬きもせずに おれたちは光の渦に巻き込まれてく
Without even blinking, we get sucked into a whirlpool of light.

193
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:14,680
宇宙の片隅に 置き去りにされて
Left behind in a corner of the universe,

194
00:27:18,060 --> 00:27:21,080
照らせ 青月のキセキよ照らせ
Illuminate us, O miracle of the blue moon, illuminate us!

195
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:32,620
星がまたたきディスタンス 寂しがりやたちの伝説さ
Stars blinking in the distance, the legend of the lonely ones.

196
00:27:33,560 --> 00:27:40,120
ワンナイトカーニバル ファイッ！
One Night Carnival! Fight!

197
00:28:22,919 --> 00:28:29,339
キャサリンに恋うファナティクスが 俺の胸を締め付ける
Fanatics in love with Catherine tighten their grip on my chest.

198
00:28:31,179 --> 00:28:35,519
矢田さんが言った言葉を 確かに俺たちは聞いたんだ
The words Yada-san said, we definitely heard them.

199
00:28:36,439 --> 00:28:39,559
天使！Can you master baby? Master baby!
Angel! Can you master baby? Master baby!

200
00:28:39,899 --> 00:28:42,859
Can you master baby? Master baby!

201
00:28:43,479 --> 00:28:46,519
Can you master baby? Master baby! Be my baby!

202
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:50,699
Can you master baby? Master baby, alone!

203
00:28:57,159 --> 00:29:04,819
おれたちが探るタブーになんて訳なんてなかったよ ただ少しだけ 勇気を出したかもしれない
There was no reason for the taboos we explored; maybe we just mustered a little courage.

204
00:29:07,459 --> 00:29:11,099
恋いしているのさ この夜に恋いしてるのさ
We're in love, we're in love with this night!

205
00:29:11,279 --> 00:29:17,939
やがて海が見える 寂しがりやたちの伝説さ
Soon the sea will appear, the legend of the lonely ones.

206
00:29:19,159 --> 00:29:25,539
ワンナイトカーニバル ファイッ！
One Night Carnival! Fight!

207
00:29:31,239 --> 00:29:34,639
あの頃の俺たち 闇の中じゃなきゃ夢見られなかった！
Back then, we couldn't dream unless it was in the darkness!

208
00:29:36,119 --> 00:29:42,699
あのミラーボールみたいに 明るくて真っ直ぐな美しさに 憧れてたからさ
Because we longed for a beauty as bright and straight as that mirror ball.

209
00:29:44,359 --> 00:29:47,979
行こうぜ ピリアードの向こうへ！
Let's go, beyond the pillars!

210
00:29:50,439 --> 00:29:57,199
もうすぐ海が見える 寂しがりやたちの伝説さ
Soon the sea will appear, the legend of the lonely ones.

211
00:30:00,599 --> 00:30:05,919
ワンナイトカーニバル ファイッ！
One Night Carnival! Fight!

212
00:34:39,850 --> 00:34:43,600
はい！というわけで、今日はね、の準備もOKなので、
Yes! So, today, our preparations are all set, so...

213
00:34:44,020 --> 00:34:49,890
今日はね、ゲストを呼ぶかな？じゃあ呼びましょう！
Today, should we invite our guests? Let's call them out!

214
00:34:46,030 --> 00:34:52,490
オッケー！ゲスト、カモン！
Okay! Guests, come on!

215
00:34:52,490 --> 00:35:03,839
カモン！
Come on!

216
00:35:06,472 --> 00:35:09,292
おいしいじゃん！甘いけどすっぱいもち米のやつ？
It's good! It's sweet and sour, like sticky rice?

217
00:35:09,502 --> 00:35:11,332
そう！これね、発酵食品なの！
That's right! It's a fermented food!

218
00:35:11,502 --> 00:35:12,972
え、これ発酵食品なの！？
Eh, this is fermented?!

219
00:35:12,972 --> 00:35:13,972
[Text: Brem]

220
00:35:14,252 --> 00:35:17,352
でもちゃんとあの、一応ね、これお菓子なので
But you know, it's technically a snack, so...

221
00:35:17,602 --> 00:35:18,932
おかしいじゃん！
That's weird!

222
00:35:19,252 --> 00:35:21,652
えー、でもちゃんとお菓子だよ！
Eh, but it's definitely a snack!

223
00:35:22,352 --> 00:35:23,952
じゃあちょっといただきます！
Well then, let's dig in!

224
00:35:24,352 --> 00:35:26,652
あー、どう？
Ah, how is it?

225
00:35:26,852 --> 00:35:28,652
うん、うん、うん...
Mhm, mhm, mhm...

226
00:35:28,952 --> 00:35:32,252
一応ね、イオフィは苦手な味よ。
Well, to be honest, Iofi isn't a fan of this flavor.

227
00:35:32,452 --> 00:35:33,652
え？苦手なの？
Eh? You don't like it?

228
00:35:33,652 --> 00:35:35,952
あ、苦手なんだ！
Ah, she doesn't like it!

229
00:35:36,352 --> 00:35:38,052
え、美味しい！
Eh, it's delicious!

230
00:35:38,252 --> 00:35:39,352
おいしい？おいしい？
Delicious? Delicious?

231
00:35:39,652 --> 00:35:42,652
あ、でも、ほかの皆もそれ気になるんだったら、あの、どうぞ！
Ah, but if the rest of you are curious about it, well, please go ahead!

232
00:35:43,052 --> 00:35:44,352
あ、食べてみる！
Ah, I'll try some!

233
00:35:44,652 --> 00:35:47,352
じゃあ、食べますわ！
Well then, I'll have some!

234
00:35:47,652 --> 00:35:49,152
なんだこれ、甘いけど...
What is this, it's sweet, but...

235
00:35:49,352 --> 00:35:51,152
甘いんだ！いただきます！
It's sweet! Let's eat!

236
00:35:51,352 --> 00:35:53,652
なんかこうわ、なんかこう酸っぱみを感じる？
It has kind of a sour kick to it?

237
00:35:53,952 --> 00:35:55,152
えー！
Eh?!

238
00:35:55,352 --> 00:35:57,152
結構ね、日本で言うとね...
Actually, if you compare it to something in Japan...

239
00:35:57,352 --> 00:35:59,152
落雁にちょっと食感が近い！
The texture is a bit like rakugan!

240
00:35:59,352 --> 00:36:01,152
なるほど！
I see!

241
00:36:01,352 --> 00:36:03,352
そう、これね、一応スタッフさんも食べるんですけど
Yeah, and the staff members eat this too, but...

242
00:36:03,652 --> 00:36:06,152
正直、スタッフさんから言うと、なんか甘酒っぽい味の...
Honestly, according to the staff, it tastes kind of like amazake...

243
00:36:06,452 --> 00:36:07,952
確かに！
True!

244
00:36:08,252 --> 00:36:09,652
はい。ちょっと...さっき、わかるって言ってたんだけど
Yeah. Wait... you said earlier that you understood it, right?

245
00:36:09,952 --> 00:36:11,652
全然嘘でした！
That was a complete lie!

246
00:36:11,952 --> 00:36:14,152
全然違う味だった！すみません！
It tasted completely different! Sorry!

247
00:36:14,352 --> 00:36:15,652
そんなことある？
Is that even possible?

248
00:36:15,952 --> 00:36:17,652
じゃあ、これが初めてということね？初めて。どうだ？
So this is your first time trying it? Your first time. How is it?

249
00:36:17,952 --> 00:36:18,952
おいしい？
Is it good?

250
00:36:19,152 --> 00:36:21,652
え、なんか不思議だなー、これ。不思議！
Eh, it's kind of mysterious, this. So mysterious!

251
00:36:21,952 --> 00:36:23,652
甘口？
Sweet?

252
00:36:23,952 --> 00:36:25,652
甘酸っぱい？
Sweet and sour?

253
00:36:25,952 --> 00:36:27,152
甘酸っぱいよ！
It's sweet and sour!

254
00:36:27,452 --> 00:36:29,152
うん、でもね、自分的なこのパサパサ感は...
Yeah, but personally, I'm not really a fan of the crumbly texture...

255
00:36:29,352 --> 00:36:30,652
あまり好きじゃなかったから。
...because I didn't like it that much.

256
00:36:30,952 --> 00:36:32,652
そうじゃない、好きじゃないのも持ってきてる！
That's right, she brought things she doesn't even like!

257
00:36:32,952 --> 00:36:34,652
そう、好き嫌い関係なくっていっぱい、
Yeah, regardless of likes and dislikes, she brought lots of them!

258
00:36:34,952 --> 00:36:37,152
確かに！好きじゃないのも持ってきている！
That's true! She brought things she doesn't even like!

259
00:36:37,352 --> 00:36:39,652
おもてなしありがとうございます！ありがとうございます！
Thank you for the hospitality! Thank you very much!

260
00:36:39,952 --> 00:36:41,652
お疲れ様です！
Good work!

261
00:36:41,952 --> 00:36:44,152
はい、じゃあ、次に行きますか？
All right, shall we move on to the next one?

262
00:36:44,452 --> 00:36:45,952
雪花ラミィから？雪花ラミィから！
From Yukihana Lamy? From Yukihana Lamy!

263
00:36:46,252 --> 00:36:48,152
行くよ！
Here we go!

264
00:36:48,352 --> 00:36:50,152
やった！オッケー！
Yay! Okay!

265
00:36:50,452 --> 00:36:52,152
好きな数字があるんだ。
There's a number she likes.

266
00:36:52,452 --> 00:36:54,152
なんだ？好きな数字？
What is it? Her favorite number?

267
00:36:54,452 --> 00:36:56,152
好きな数字は？
What's your favorite number?

268
00:36:56,452 --> 00:36:58,152
誰だって思う？
Who do you think it is?

269
00:36:58,452 --> 00:37:00,152
めんどくせえ！
What a pain!

270
00:37:00,452 --> 00:37:02,152
何番だ？
What number is it?

271
00:37:02,452 --> 00:37:04,152
4番！
Number 4!

272
00:37:04,452 --> 00:37:06,152
違う！
Wrong!

273
00:37:06,452 --> 00:37:08,152
6！ 6！ 6！ 6！
6! 6! 6! 6!

274
00:37:08,452 --> 00:37:10,152
誕生日がね、6月だからね！
Because her birthday is in June, right!

275
00:37:10,452 --> 00:37:12,152
ツノっぽいからね！
Because of the horns, right!

276
00:37:12,452 --> 00:37:14,152
ツノっぽいから6！
6 because it looks like a horn!

277
00:37:14,452 --> 00:37:16,152
じゃあ、ツノっぽいから6ね、大正解！
So 6 because it looks like a horn, correct!

278
00:37:16,452 --> 00:37:18,152
そして！
And then!

279
00:37:18,452 --> 00:37:20,152
そして、6番！
And number 6!

280
00:37:20,452 --> 00:37:22,152
オープン！
Open!

281
00:37:22,452 --> 00:37:24,152
[Text: Tamarind]

282
00:37:24,452 --> 00:37:26,152
なんじゃこれ？
What on earth is this?

283
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:28,152
これね、タマリンド！
This is tamarind!

284
00:37:28,452 --> 00:37:30,152
タマリンド！
Tamarind!

285
00:37:30,452 --> 00:37:32,152
え、これは？
Eh, what is this?

286
00:37:32,452 --> 00:37:34,152
お菓子？
A snack?

287
00:37:34,452 --> 00:37:36,152
お菓子ですね。
It's a snack.

288
00:37:36,452 --> 00:37:38,152
じゃあ、いただきます！
Well then, let's eat!

289
00:37:38,452 --> 00:37:40,152
うーん...
Mmm...

290
00:37:40,452 --> 00:37:42,152
酸っぱい！
It's sour!

291
00:37:42,452 --> 00:37:44,152
酸っぱいね！
It is sour!

292
00:37:44,452 --> 00:37:46,152
でも、タマリンドはね、インドネシアでは...
But tamarind, in Indonesia...

293
00:37:46,452 --> 00:37:48,152
あ、そうなんだ！
Ah, is that right!

294
00:37:48,452 --> 00:37:50,152
酸っぱくて甘い。
It's sour and sweet.

295
00:37:50,452 --> 00:37:52,152
美味しいよ！
It's delicious!

296
00:37:52,452 --> 00:37:54,152
じゃあ、みんなもどうぞ！
Well then, everyone have some too!

297
00:37:54,452 --> 00:37:56,152
いただきます！
Let's eat!

298
00:37:56,452 --> 00:37:58,152
うわ、酸っぱい！
Woah, it's sour!

299
00:37:58,452 --> 00:38:00,152
酸っぱい！
It's sour!

300
00:38:00,452 --> 00:38:02,152
でも、美味しい！
But it's good!

301
00:38:02,452 --> 00:38:04,152
そうだね！
That's right!

302
00:38:04,452 --> 00:38:06,152
じゃあ、次に行きましょう！
Well then, let's move on to the next one!

303
00:40:06,296 --> 00:40:09,626
ショット行く？ショットいこう。あ、はい、はい。
Shall we go with a shot? Let's go with a shot. Ah, yes, yes.

304
00:40:09,826 --> 00:40:12,296
うわ、ちょっと。チャキッ、チャキッ。
Woah, wait a minute. *Clack, clack*.

305
00:40:12,496 --> 00:40:15,296
すごーい！すごーい、すごい！
Wow! That's amazing, amazing!

306
00:40:15,496 --> 00:40:18,296
いいよ、いいよ、いいよ。あ、大丈夫？
It's fine, it's fine, it's fine. Ah, are you okay?

307
00:40:18,496 --> 00:40:21,296
ナプキンいらない？大丈夫？え、でもペーパーはある。
You don't need a napkin? Are you okay? Uh, but we have paper.

308
00:40:21,496 --> 00:40:25,296
ペーパーいるか？ちょっと、そっちにの、なんか袋は...
Do you need paper? Wait, over there, the bag is...

309
00:40:25,496 --> 00:40:28,296
かわいいのに入った！かわいい！かわいい！
It came in a cute one! Cute! Cute!

310
00:40:28,496 --> 00:40:32,296
嘘でしょ？えー、さすがに？なんか、え？臭？臭い？
No way? Seriously? What, huh? Does it smell? Does it smell?

